<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02468</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6da3c03e-d5b9-4177-9a52-0a6c07117068</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Explain the steps and complete some missing steps for deriving the quadratic formula.</item>
        <item>Explain how the quadratic formula is related to the process of completing the square for a quadratic equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>9.8.1: Deriving the Quadratic Formula, Part 1 <list id="list-00003">
            <item>In this activity, you learned how to derive the quadratic formula by completing the square for a quadratic equation without evaluating some of the numerical expressions along the way.</item>
            <item>9.8.1: Self Check</item>
            <item>9.8.1: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>9.8.2: Deriving the Quadratic Formula, Part 2 <list id="list-00004">
            <item>In this activity, you studied a series of steps to solve <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> by completing the square and making sense of how it leads to the quadratic formula.</item>
            <item>9.8.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>9.8.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>9.8.3: Understanding That the Quadratic Formula Is the Combined Steps of Completing the Square <list id="list-00005">
            <item>In this activity, you had to explain parts of a solution for solving an equation by completing the square, where each step was shown, but numerical expressions were not evaluated.</item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
      <list id="list-00006">
        <item>9.8.4: Practice</item>
      </list>
      <note class="checking-in" id="sect-00002">
        <title>Checking In</title>
        <exercise id="_2a5c54e7-f775-4ff8-9390-23f82d611955" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>